### army-memorandum-class ###
# Built example PDFs. These are generated output, not sources: the golden files
# under examples/golden/ are this repo's tracked rendered reference.
# Note the narrow glob -- DODb1.pdf is a build *input* and stays tracked, as
# does examples/assets/placeholder-seal.pdf, which the glob also never matches.
examples/example*.pdf

# Harness scratch directory (diffs and per-build extractions).
.test-work/

# latexindent's cruft directory -- backup files and indent.log, routed here by
# `-c` in the format/lint tasks so they do not land in the repo root.
.latexindent/

# Local review notes. POST-0.4.0-REVIEW.md is a working document for the
# maintainer's own later review, not part of the repository's documentation and
# deliberately not part of any PR. Ignored so that a `git add -A` cannot sweep it
# in -- which is exactly what happened once before this rule existed.
POST-*-REVIEW.md

# go-task's fingerprint cache. `task` stores a checksum per task here to decide
# what is up to date; it is derived state and rebuilds itself. Deleting it just
# forces one full rebuild.
.task/

# Downloaded reference material -- the regulation this class implements, the
# figures extracted from it, and any related DoD/DA publications or templates.
# These are downloaded references, not sources and not build inputs, and each is
# reissued on its own schedule. So the tree carries a tracked index of stable
# record-page URLs (references/README.md) rather than the binaries themselves.
#
# The trailing /* is load-bearing: git does not descend into an ignored
# directory, so `references/` plus a negation would hide README.md along with
# everything else. Ignoring the *contents* is what leaves the negation reachable.
#
# Deliberately scoped: DODb1.pdf at the repo root, and
# examples/assets/placeholder-seal.pdf, are build *inputs* and stay tracked --
# which is why this file still has no blanket *.pdf rule.
references/*
!references/README.md
